    <h1>Churches</h1>
    <p class="lead">The parish churches of the ARCH Benefice serve the Lenches and their neighbours, with several other congregations a short drive away in Evesham.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="arch">
    <h2>The ARCH Benefice</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="mt0">The parishes of <strong>A</strong>bbots Morton, <strong>R</strong>ous Lench, <strong>C</strong>hurch Lench and <strong>H</strong>arvington — which give the benefice its name — were brought together in 2001, within the Diocese of Worcester.</p>
      <p>St Egwin's at Norton &amp; Lenchwick is also listed among the benefice churches, though Church of England records still place that parish formally within the Evesham benefice.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://www.archbenefice.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit the ARCH Benefice website</a></p>
    </div>

    <table class="contacts">
      <caption>Churches of the benefice</caption>
